# D19 decision: DEADLAUNCH, tests/test_host_bridge_transitions.py, tests/test_project_advisor_pairing.py (Astra for the orchestrator, 2026-10-17)

Decision: LAND

- `tests/test_host_bridge_transitions.py`: Removes the lifecycle caller’s reconciliation, exact-readback, single-call, owner-version and unobserved-callback assertions (`canon/main:tests/test_host_bridge_transitions.py:149–161`). Their subject, `PortfolioLifecycleIntegration._run_schedule`, is deleted with the module (`canon/main:src/otto/portfolio/lifecycle.py:333`), as required by `projects/program/tasklist.md:149` and `ops/prework/DEADLAUNCH.md:9`. Supported bridge checks remain unchanged: pause/resume (`tests/test_host_bridge_transitions.py:50–65`), scope/CAS rejection (`:126–134`) and recovery without duplicate updates (`:136–146`). Those assertions still fail when the corresponding supported behavior breaks.
- `tests/test_project_advisor_pairing.py`: Removes assertions that the retired lifecycle dispatcher forwards advisor generation `2` and assignment `ADVISOR` (`canon/main:tests/test_project_advisor_pairing.py:142–168`). The corresponding `_deliver_role` implementation is deleted (`canon/main:src/otto/portfolio/lifecycle.py:491`), matching the row’s explicit retirement of this class and its tests. Independent generation, exact conversation and stale/wrong-recipient assertions remain (`tests/test_project_advisor_pairing.py:56–73`); supported manager-question delivery still checks the exact advisor, completion and suppression of replay (`tests/test_project_advisor_delivery.py:162–179`). These retain meaningful failure conditions for supported advisor behavior.

The supplied `ops/runs/DEADLAUNCH/land.out` was absent. The two-file list was independently reconstructed using the gate’s selection predicate (`ops/bootstrap/land.sh:130–137`). This decision covers D19 only; no tests were run.